    {
      "path": "src/coordinators/workspace/restore.ts",
      "content": "When the activating hook throws on a first-run restore, `inRoot` correctly aborts and rethrows, but this branch exits without discarding the prepared candidate. Unlike the existing-workspace branch below, the candidate database and its root registration remain after the failed apply. Catch activation failures here, discard the candidate, and rethrow; extend the first-run fault test to assert that no candidate remains.",
      "existing_code": "          const activation = await persistence.activateFirstCandidate(token.candidateId, deps.restoreHooks?.activating);",
      "start_line": 858,
      "end_line": 858,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/coordinators/workspace/restore-faults.test.ts",
      "content": "Both hold tests assume the hook is reached within 50 ms, although preparation and activation perform multiple asynchronous database operations first. A slower CI runner can fail these tests despite correct behavior. Have the hook resolve a separate 'entered' promise and await that before checking the pending operation; release the gate in a finally block so failed assertions do not leave the restore held.",
      "existing_code": "const settled = () =\u003e new Promise((resolve) =\u003e setTimeout(resolve, 50));",
      "start_line": 26,
      "end_line": 26,
      "category": "test",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/delivery/faults.ts",
      "content": "`backup:read` does not fail when all exported stores are empty: `readExportSnapshot` only invokes `onBatch` for nonempty rows, so this callback is never reached and `runExport` can return `Built` and offer a download. This can occur when exporting a recovery database containing metadata but no authoritative records. Ensure the injected read failure also covers the zero-record snapshot (for example, fail from `onStart` when all counts are zero), and add a test for that case.",
      "existing_code": "              readExportSnapshot(indexedDB, database, layout, () =\u003e {\n                throw new Error('injected fault: backup:read');\n              }, onStart),",
      "start_line": 150,
      "end_line": 152,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
  ],
